ene expression  scores  were significantly higher at baseline  compared with non-responders  as shown in panel b highlighting the  association between response to t-cell  engagers such as flotituzumab  and the t-cell inflamed tumor  microenvironment  we also identified a set of genes that  were differentially expressed  between patients with tp53 abnormalities  and those with p53 wild type aml  and that were associated with response  to flooded system up  interestingly cd8b was the top ranking  gene  associated with response with an artwork  value  of 0.879 as shown in panel b  and finally flow cytometry experiments  performed by  mike reddick at university of washington  using bone marrow samples from  patients on study showed a trend towards  higher percentages  of cda t cells in individuals with  mutations of tp53  therefore validating the transatomic  findings of this study  so just to conclude my talk immune  transphotomic analysis of in silico  and white lab cohorts of tp53 mutated  aml  suggests the presence of high t cell  infiltration and high expression of  immune checkpoints  and interferon gamma signaling molecules  compare with aml subgroups with  other risk defining molecular lesions  experimentally derived tp53 related  immune gene signatures  are significant for survival prediction  in aml  our translational study has shown that  immunotherapy with flotissus map  has efficacy in individuals with altered  tp53 status  with an overall reduction of bone marrow  blasts averaging  15.2 percent and overall sorry 51.2  percent at an overall response rate of  60  we believe that these findings encourage  further studies of flotivisumab in  larger cohorts of patients who harbor  this molecular lesion so this is my  acknowledgement slide i wish to express  my thanks to co-authors  collaborators from many different many  institutions around the world and also  funding  sources i will be very happy to take  questions if you  do not mind emailing me thank you ver